   "validatorKey": "y10_1_3_l1_exam_kib",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Exam Question: Bytes to Kibibytes</h2><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Cambridge IGCSE 0478/12, June 2025, Question 2(b). A student has an image file stored on their computer. The size of the image file is 3072 bytes.</p><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y10-13l1-exam-kib-a\">(i) Give the size of the image file in kibibytes (KiB). [1]</label><input id=\"y10-13l1-exam-kib-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-kib-a\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Bytes to Kibibytes part a\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y10-13l1-exam-kib-b\">(ii) State the number of nibbles in 1 byte. [1]</label><input id=\"y10-13l1-exam-kib-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"exam-kib-b\" aria-label=\"Exam Question: Bytes to Kibibytes part b\" autocomplete=\"off\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y10-13l1-exam-kib-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y10-13l1-exam-kib-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div>"
